%I A401464 #5 Nov 02 2026 15:40:12
%S A401464 1,4,22,278,4005,66346
%N A401464 Number of one-sided (equivalently, free) polyforms with n cells in the honeycomb of the 17-faced Voronoi cell of the point (1/8, 1/8, 1/8) under space group I4_132 (No. 214), whose orbit is the vertex set of the Laves graph.
%C A401464 The cell is the 17-faced space-filling polyhedron (4^6 5^6 6^2 8^3 faces, f-vector (30, 45, 17)) that is the Voronoi cell of the vertex set of the Laves graph (the srs net), i.e. of Wyckoff position 8a of space group I4_132 (No. 214), generating point (1/8, 1/8, 1/8), site symmetry .32; its honeycomb has 4 cell types (translation classes), each cell with 17 face-neighbors. Polyforms are face-connected clusters of cells, counted up to lattice translation and the proper (orientation-preserving) symmetries of the honeycomb.
%C A401464 The honeycomb is chiral (all honeycomb symmetries are proper), so the one-sided and free counts coincide.
%C A401464 The symmetry group G of the tiling has order 24 modulo lattice translations (all 24 proper), and the counts satisfy the Burnside identity |G|*free(n) = Sum_g Fix_g(n).
%D A401464 Alan H. Schoen, On the Graph (10-3)-a, Notices Amer. Math. Soc. 55 (2008), no. 6, 663.
%H A401464 H. S. M. Coxeter, <a href="https://doi.org/10.4153/CJM-1955-003-7">On Laves' graph of girth ten</a>, Canad. J. Math. 7 (1955), 18-23.
%H A401464 Tyler Satchel Orden, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22502081">plesiohedron-census: certified space-filling polyhedra from a gated agentic search (code, certificates, catalog)</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A401464 Moritz W. Schmitt, <a href="https://doi.org/10.17169/refubium-14374">On Space Groups and Dirichlet-Voronoi Stereohedra</a>, Dissertation, Freie Universität Berlin, 2016 (table for No. 214, f-vector (30, 45, 17) at (1/8, 1/8, 1/8)).
